flf2a$ 5 3 65 -1 28 0 0 3983

Beyond Neo FIGfont by Philippe Majerus (http://www.phm.lu/), monochrome version (phm-beyondneo-mono.flf).
This font supports the ISO 8859-1 and Windows 1252 Latin-1, and MS-DOS 437, 737, 850, and 866 character sets, and more.
This font uses Unicode 13.0 characters (sextants and smooth sextants), and a few Unicode 16.0 (semicircles, a few octants).
It does not require an ANSI/VT terminal (does not use escape sequences) and works fine with FIGlet,
but the terminal must support the Unicode 13.0 Symbols for Legacy Computing block.

Included characters:
• Latin
   • Latin-1 (Basic Latin and Latin-1 Supplement blocks)
   • Latin Extended-A
   • Latin Extended-B
   • Latin Extended Additional
• Greek
• Cyrillic (all capitals)
• Japanese Katakana (half-width and full-width), Hiragana as Katakana, 153 Kanji (mostly for numbers and dates, places)
• Some mathematical operators and symbols
• Double-Struck Capitals and Digits (requires Unicode 16.0 Symbols for Legacy Computing extensions and supplement)
• Number Forms
• Control Pictures
• Braille patterns
• Miscellaneous (extra symbols, outlined capital letters and numbers, segmented digits, emojis …)

Remember to use "figlet -C utf8" to access Unicode characters.
This font does not support "smushing" (-S) and large characters will get mangled, and "kerning" (-k) has no effect.

Date: September 2024 - August 2026

